hosting/.firebase/

# Docs (local working notes, some contain API keys)
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/` so a subdirectory can be re-included below: git never
# descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a bare `docs/` makes any later `!docs/...`
# rule unreachable.
docs/*
# Business-sensitive pricing/geo-growth strategy — keep out of public repo even if docs/ is ever un-ignored
docs/pricing-strategy.md

# Exception: /healthcheck snapshots are tracked. They are the baseline the skill diffs each
# run against — untracked, they live in exactly one working copy and a reinstall loses the
# history. Scanned before un-ignoring (2026-08-06): no API keys, tokens or private keys;
# third-party account names, user ids and IP/subnet strings are redacted. The owner's own
# address stays as-is — it is already the public author email on every commit here.
# Everything else under docs/healthcheck/ (report.html, seen.json) stays ignored.
!docs/healthcheck/
docs/healthcheck/*
!docs/healthcheck/snapshot-*.json
SECURITY.md
SECURITY_DELIVERY_SUMMARY.txt

# Generated/vendored stubs in root (not project source)
/commonMain/

# Temp images in root (move to proper location)
*.png
!composeApp/**/*.png
!iosApp/**/*.png
!core/**/*.png
!feature/**/*.png
*.stackdump

# Gisti MCP secrets — never commit (public repo)
client_secret_*.json
**/client_secret_*.json
**/*-sa.json
**/service-account*.json

# mcp-server dev/build (never commit)
.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars
**/node_modules/

# local wrangler dev log
*.wrangler-dev.log
mcp-publisher.exe
mcp-server/mcp-publisher.exe

# JVM crash dumps — HotSpot drops these next to whatever cwd the daemon had. Never source,
# and this repo is PUBLIC: a heap/stack dump added by `git add -A` is published for good.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
